# Repos the explorer suite needs checked out BESIDE it on the CI venue.
#
# Declaring a sibling here is what makes its cross-repo guards actually run. An
# UNdeclared sibling is not a neutral omission: every guard written against it
# resolves with existsSync, calls this.skip(), and the gate still prints PASS,
# so the run reports green having exercised none of them. Measured 2026-08-12,
# that gap was 13 guards (a venue carrying only indexer + vm + sdk ran 2431
# passing / 18 pending where a full local checkout runs 2444 / 5). See
# test/unit/sibling-coverage.test.js, which reports the surface this file leaves
# uncovered; the same gap applies to a sibling that is declared but missing.
#
# ci-dispatch.sh ships each of these at its origin/master (falling back to local
# HEAD) and REFUSES the push if one is not a checkout beside this repo, so a
# declared sibling can never be silently absent.

# Indexer schema conformance, list-edit resolution and reorg DDL, and the
# hub-connector contract.
xchain-indexer
# Contract endpoints, the node-engine ceiling, and vm-query parity.
xchain-vm
# Checkpoint, locked-balance and contract-state proof parity.
xchain-sdk
# Decoder schema conformance and the mempool decode twin.
xchain-decoder
# Action-manifest, consensus-primitive and vm-query constant conformance.
xchain-documentation
# Compression-parameter twin parity.
xchain-encoder
# Vendored coins-registry byte-identity: BTC/LTC/DOGE/index/consensus_pin.
xchain-hub
